Take the pusher off the store while it is still a process.

The exit hook was registered with on_proc_exit, which runs after
shmem_exit. By then ProcKill has handed this process's PGPROC back and
MyProcNumber is INVALID_PROC_NUMBER, so the ConditionVariableBroadcast
at the top of the hook is a broadcast without a proc number to speak
for. It pushes a sentinel whose procno is -1, the wakeup list encodes
empty as -1 too, and so proclist_is_empty says the list is empty while
proclist_contains, reading the PGPROC one slot before the array, says
the sentinel is still in it. That loop has no way out.

What that costs is not one worker. The hook never reaches zou_wal_close,
so the writer lease keeps being renewed by the heartbeat thread of a
cluster that is gone, at a full core, for as long as the machine is up.
A node restoring the same store gets a fresh holder id, is refused every
second for a minute, and stops its own postmaster. That is the whole of
zou #503: on the crash loop the takeover was tried and correctly
refused, because the predecessor was still alive and still renewing.

Registered with before_shmem_exit instead, the hook runs while the
process still has a PGPROC, the broadcast is an ordinary broadcast, the
store is closed and the lease released, and the next incarnation takes
it without waiting at all.

The page service's hook stays on on_proc_exit. It only stops threads in
the shim and touches no shared memory.

See zou #503.

--- a/src/backend/access/transam/zou_wal.c
+++ b/src/backend/access/transam/zou_wal.c
@@ -311,6 +311,14 @@
 	 * Say so before the store goes, and wake everyone waiting on a
 	 * durable LSN. Nothing publishes one after this, so a waiter that
 	 * sleeps through the exit is a waiter that never wakes.
+	 *
+	 * This is a before_shmem_exit callback and has to stay one. A
+	 * condition variable is only safe to touch while this process still
+	 * has a PGPROC, and after shmem_exit its proc number is
+	 * INVALID_PROC_NUMBER, which is the same -1 an empty wakeup list
+	 * holds. A broadcast from there pushes a sentinel it can never see
+	 * leave and spins on that forever, at a full core, with the close
+	 * below never reached (zou #503).
 	 */
 	ZouWalShmem->pusher_pid = 0;
 	ConditionVariableBroadcast(&ZouWalShmem->durable_cv);
@@ -454,7 +462,7 @@
 						 1000, PG_WAIT_EXTENSION);
 		ResetLatch(MyLatch);
 	}
-	on_proc_exit(zou_wal_on_exit, (Datum) 0);
+	before_shmem_exit(zou_wal_on_exit, (Datum) 0);
 
 	/*
 	 * On a store that already holds WAL, restart right after its last
